              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. Sliding sections need clearance to slide, and that clearance becomes flex under load, so a telescoping ladder always moves more than a conventional extension ladder of the same length. What you gain is storage and transport, which is why the format exists.
